  "details": "Currently VRChat allows you to assign a unique mic in desktop mode and VR, however this is somewhat half baked in it's current form.\n\nThe biggest issue is the fact that in desktop and VR mode one would have entirely different microphones, and not all microphones are made equal. As such, I need different microphone settings in VR and desktop. Currently, these are not separate, and it means that sometimes when I move from desktop to VR and vice-versa, I will be using incorrect microphone settings, giving me a worse cut-off etc.\n\nCould the Mic output volume, noise suppression, and mic activation threshold be separate between desktop and VR mode? Additionally, if for whatever reason, one is using the same microphone in both VR and desktop, the settings should sync (as an edge case).",
